You are a senior product designer + senior frontend engineer at a modern startup.

I am building my first internship project and I want the frontend to look production-ready, premium, and impressive enough to demonstrate to a CEO.

PROJECT NAME:
SkillBarter

PROJECT TAGLINE:
"Your Skills. Your Community. Your Currency."

CORE PROBLEM STATEMENT:
"Hyperlocal Community Service & Skill Barter: A geo-fenced social network connecting neighbors to trade physical skills (e.g., plumbing for web design or painting for carpentry) with zero cash exchange, governed by a community trust score."

IMPORTANT PRODUCT IDEA:
This is similar to LinkedIn in terms of social-network structure:
- User profiles
- Feed
- Connections
- Messaging
- Notifications
- Search
- Skill profiles
- Reputation

BUT IT IS NOT A PROFESSIONAL JOB NETWORK.

The audience is different:
- Local residents
- Students
- Freelancers
- Skilled workers
- Hobbyists
- Home-service providers
- People who want to learn skills
- People who want help from nearby people

The core purpose is:
"Connect nearby people so they can exchange skills/services without money."

Example:
Person A knows Web Development but needs plumbing help.
Person B knows Plumbing but needs a website.
They can barter their skills instead of exchanging money.

Build ONLY THE FRONTEND for now.
Use realistic mock data and mock interactions.
Structure the application cleanly so a real backend/API can be integrated later.

